@startuml
title Safehome Security Function State Diagram

state Startup {
  [*] --> Checking

  state Checking
  Checking : do / check everything during startup

  state ReadyToUse
  ReadyToUse : do / become ready to use if no problems found

  state Resetting
  Resetting : do / allow user to reset when it is ready to use

  state Activating
  Activating : do / allow user to activate when it is ready to use
    Activating --> Monitoring: [valid] user activates system

  state TurningOff
  TurningOff : do / allow user to turn off when it is ready to use
    TurningOff --> [*]: user turns off system
}

state Monitoring {
  state Normal
  Normal : do / continue monitoring if no alarms

  state AlarmActive
  AlarmActive : do / start alarm and send alerts if sensor triggered

  state FalseAlarm
  FalseAlarm : do / continue monitoring if false alarm
    FalseAlarm --> Normal: [valid] no more alarms or time ended

  state TimeEnded
  TimeEnded : do / continue monitoring if time ends
    TimeEnded --> Normal: [valid] time did not end

  Normal --> AlarmActive: [valid] sensor triggered
}

state Password {
  state WaitingForPassword
  WaitingForPassword : do / wait for user input at any time
    WaitingForPassword --> PasswordEntered: password entered

  state PasswordEntered
  PasswordEntered : do / check entered password
    PasswordEntered --> WaitingForPassword: [invalid] incorrect password
    PasswordEntered --> Monitoring: [valid] user enters the correct password
}

Startup --> Monitoring: no problems during startup and system activated
Monitoring --> Password: alarm triggered or system turned off
Password --> Monitoring
@enduml
